    "description": "Do you want to build the data foundation for a fleet of batteries, from the lab to the field? This role sits where data engineering, software, and the physical sciences meet. You will stand up, nearly from scratch, the pipelines and platforms that carry sensor, test lab, fleet, and model training data across the organization. Every model, algorithm, and design decision we make depends on that data being complete, trustworthy, and easy to use. You will work side by side with scientists, software engineers, and cell experts, and as an early hire you will define how data works across the organization.<br/><br/>This role can be based in Boston, Irvine, Sunnyvale, or Seattle, and involves occasional domestic travel, up to 10% of the time.<br/><br/><br/>Key job responsibilities<br/>\u2022 Design and build the data architecture for sensor, test lab, fleet, and model training data, from ingestion through storage and access.<br/>\u2022 Build scalable, reliable pipelines for high-volume time-series data from devices and test equipment.<br/>\u2022 Own data quality, lineage, and governance, so scientists and engineers can trust and reproduce their results.<br/>\u2022 Work with scientists and engineers across algorithms, ML, cell modeling, and testing to understand their needs and deliver data in forms they can use.<br/>\u2022 Set data engineering standards and tools, and help grow the data engineering function as the organization expands.<br/><br/><br/>A day in the life<br/>Your week moves between design, code, and the people who use your data. One day you might be designing how years of cycling data from multiple labs land in one consistent schema, and the next tracking down why a field data feed is dropping samples. You could be working with a scientist on the data a new model needs, or reviewing a pipeline design with the software team. Some of the best days will be when a scientist finds an aging signal in data your pipeline made usable. Your work determines how fast everyone else can learn.<br/><br/>About the team<br/>We are building Amazon's energy storage capability, providing power for advanced technologies while contributing to a stable grid. Our product is highly connected, yet secure and resilient by design. We own it end to end, from software, ML, and controls through system design to cell selection and supply, and on to a safety-certified product in the field. The organization operates like a startup inside Amazon: small, fast-moving, and accountable for our decisions. We work across hardware, software, and science, with suppliers and partners worldwide, and with Amazon infrastructure, procurement, legal, and finance.<br/>The organization is at an early stage and growing quickly. You will be among the first hires in your function, so you will help shape how we design, build, certify, and ship, with a direct line of sight to the product and business decisions your work informs. This is a dynamic role that will regularly present new challenges as the product and organization evolve.<br/>",
